<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Schule Schloss Salem</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1920–</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Schule Schloss Salem is a boarding school in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, founded in 1920 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-maximilian-of-baden">Prince Maximilian of Baden</a> and the educator <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurt-hahn">Kurt Hahn</a> in the former imperial abbey of Salem. Its teaching aimed to build character and civic responsibility through community service, outdoor challenge and pupil self-government. Hahn carried its ideas to Gordonstoun in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> after fleeing the Nazis, and it remains one of Germany's best-known boarding schools.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/schule-schloss-salem.jpg" alt="Schule Schloss Salem" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Janobi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schloss_Salem.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
